      'A genuine research bet needs real curiosity and stamina, not just comfort with the idea of a "Dr." prefix or family pressure toward prestige.',
    ],
  },
];

const govJobRows = [
  {
    route: 'ICAR (agriculture and allied life sciences)',
    detail:
      'ICAR\'s JRF route, run through the Agricultural Scientists Recruitment Board (ASRB) and the AIEEA-PG entrance, is built primarily for BSc Agriculture graduates and pays a stipend of roughly ₹31,000/month (JRF) or ₹35,000/month (SRF) toward a funded MSc or PhD at an ICAR institute or state agricultural university. If your BSc is in Botany, Zoology, or a related allied-science subject rather than Agriculture, verify the current year\'s eligible-subject list before assuming direct entry.',
  },
  {
    route: 'DRDO (CEPTAM Senior Technical Assistant-B)',
    detail:
      'DRDO\'s CEPTAM exam accepts a Bachelor\'s degree in Science for the STA-B post, commonly listing Chemistry, Physics, Mathematics, and Computer Science among eligible subjects. The age band is typically 18-28. Life-science subjects are not always on every year\'s list, so check the specific vacancy notification before preparing.',
  },
  {
    route: 'CSIR national laboratories (Technical Assistant)',
    detail:
