    body:
      'Starting pay for a biotech BSc lab technician typically runs around ₹3-6 LPA. The work is procedural — sample handling, documentation, and instrument operation — and it is a real way to build the lab experience that many government postings later require.',
  },
  {
    label: 'QC / QA',
    title: 'Quality control and quality assurance are the most common entry doors in pharma manufacturing',
    body:
      'Fresher QC pay usually sits around ₹2.5-4 LPA, and QA/QC Officer roles around ₹3-5.5 LPA, rising to roughly ₹8-14 LPA with several years of experience and a track record of compliance and audit work.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Industry roles',
    title: 'Production, regulatory support, and documentation roles inside pharma and biotech firms',
