  },
  {
    label: 'Food and environmental testing',
    title: 'Real sectors, but not always fresher-friendly on day one',
    body:
      'FSSAI\'s own Food Analyst route typically asks for around three years of relevant experience in food analysis after your BSc — postgraduate or research years do not count toward it. Treat food and environmental testing as a strong mid-career move once you have built lab hours, not an immediate first job.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Clinical research',
    title: 'Clinical Research Associate, Clinical Data Manager, or pharmacovigilance roles at CROs',
    body:
      'This is one of the most direct fresher routes for a life-science BSc. Fresher pay in clinical research commonly runs ₹3.5-6.5 LPA, and India\'s CRO industry — global names like IQVIA and Parexel, plus Indian CROs — is actively hiring in Bangalore, Hyderabad, and Mumbai. A short GCP (Good Clinical Practice) certification and one relevant internship noticeably improve your odds over a bare degree.',
  },
];

const bridgeCards = [
  {
    tone: 'gold',
    title: 'B.Ed: the teaching bridge',
    items: [
      'A standard B.Ed is a 2-year, NCTE-recognised programme open to any BSc graduate; a few universities now run 4-year integrated BSc-B.Ed tracks under NEP 2020.',
      'A B.Ed alone does not make you employable — you also need to clear CTET or the relevant state TET, and most schools want your science subject specialisation for classes 6-12.',
