    q: 'Is a BSc alone enough to get a good private-sector job in India?',
    a: 'Rarely on its own. Direct placement rates and starting packages for BSc-only graduates vary widely by college and vary from roughly ₹2-4 LPA at the lower end to ₹3-7 LPA at stronger colleges. What actually improves your odds is a chosen direction plus visible proof of work — a documented project, lab experience, or a relevant certification — not the degree certificate by itself.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Should I do a B.Ed or an MBA after my BSc?',
    a: 'Both are legitimate bridge routes if the daily work genuinely fits you. B.Ed suits students who want to teach and can commit to two years plus CTET or a state TET afterward. MBA suits students who want to move into healthcare, pharma, or business-side roles — any bachelor\'s degree is eligible, with CMAT, MAT, XAT, ATMA, or NMAT valid at most AICTE-approved colleges. Choose based on fit, not because it is the default next step.',
